WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:12.610
The furious rain, Makes my heart shake
hageshii ame ga, kokoro wo yuruwaseru

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:15.820
Like it did on that day
Ano hi no youni

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.910
But I just ran through, In my dream I had till yesterday
Tada hashirinuketa, kinou made no MY DREAM

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.710
...I still believe
...shinjiteiru no sa

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:34.470
I'm willing to fight, An endless defense
Owari no nai, defense demo ii yo

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:42.350
As long as you, Keep on gazing at me
Kimi ga boku wo, mitsumetsuzukete kureru nara

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:45.270
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.980
Turn to face all the mornings ahead, And someday
Ikutsumono asa wo mukae, Itsuka kitto

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.860
Try to seize them
tsukande miseru

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.450
STAND UP TO THE VICTORY!

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.120
Even if nothing, Lies on the other side
Sono mukougawa ni, nanimonakutemo

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.040
It doesn't matter to me
kamawanai kara

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:14.050
...Just as long as I can embrace, Your gentle, irreplaceable smile!
Kakegae no nai, kimi no yasashii egao daite

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.930
Üso, after taking out the mobile suit,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.500
was caught in an area under Largaine surveillance and fell into peril.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:37.030
He was saved by the Shrike Team under Oliver's command.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.030
Üso learned what it meant to wield a weapon.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:46.500
THE SHRIKE TEAM BULWARK

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.460
"The Shrike Team Bulwark".

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:49.160
THE SHRIKE TEAM BULWARK

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.300
There's also the farm,

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.930
and aren't you worried about the goat and the chickens?

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:06.860
Huh? What did you say?

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:08.660
I want to go back.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.060
Aren't you curious about my mom?

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.060
I think it'd be better to wait for her in Kasarelia.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.730
We can plant willowherb anywhere to mark where we've been.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.400
Üso, you just want to find Miss Katejina, don't you?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:25.530
No, the League Militaire people might also know about my parents...

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.300
We've finally rejoined our comrades?

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:32.730
So it would seem.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:33.930
The enemy?!

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.730
Shouldn't we prep the mobile suits?

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.860
This is D.D., the rendezvous point.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:46.960
Huh? It's a Federation mobile suit!

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.860
So, D.D. is an airfield at Bechyne.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.460
Huh, Bechyne?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.500
Here!

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.460
Here?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.060
Is this an airfield?

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.130
Looks like it.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.600
Wow! There's more over here, too!

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.430
They made it here!

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.530
I know they have factories all over the place,

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.400
but they only have three complete units?

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.360
That's not what we were told!

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:31.960
The plan was to hit the Yellow Jacket base now!

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.700
What are you talking about?

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.160
Aren't you headed into space on a Federation ship?

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.400
We're going to hit Largaine base and secure Europe's safety!

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.800
Isn't it presumptuous to think your civilian-level resistance...

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:48.830
...is a match for Zanscare's BESPA forces?

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.030
But...

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:55.630
All I'm doing is collecting your Victory-type units to take over to Ireland.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:00.560
And yet you've only managed to transport two of them?!

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.900
Thanks to you people, the Jamesguns were left behind...

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:07.500
...and the others had to go back and get them.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.300
Well, that sounds promising.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.300
This all started because of that damn fool Hangerg Ewin!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:18.730
He should've stuck to puttering around with fleet duty on Earth!

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:20.930
Now, get these things loaded!

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.660
Excuse me!

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.860
Yeah, what?

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.430
That name you just said...

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.200
Huh?

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:29.900
Hangerg Ewin. How do you know him?

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:34.430
I don't have to tell you. Can't you tell I'm busy?

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.730
How would a Earth Federation soldier know my father's name?

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.030
Oh, man...

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.360
He's still a pilot.

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:48.060
We have to rely on him, right?

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:51.260
Considering our value, they should have waited for us.

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:55.360
If you had it your way, everyone would come second to Shrike Team!

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.230
Marbet!

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.400
Should we load the mobile suits onto the transport?

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:03.230
Please do. The setters have another mission, so they'll head back.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:03.960
Yes, sir!

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.160
Do it!

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.060
Whoa, you don't want to get hit by that.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:15.730
I'm fine.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:18.430
No, you need to be careful with it. Here.

00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:19.430
Excuse me.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.560
Do you know the name Hangerg Ewin?

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.300
I'm not into new religions!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.760
Baby, I like your style!

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:31.800
Üso's looking for his father.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.060
Looks like it.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:34.700
What's wrong?

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:35.000
Excuse me, do you know the name Hangerg Ewin?

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:35.900
Nothing.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:36.260
Excuse me, do you know the name Hangerg Ewin?

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:37.600
That little...

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:41.760
Huh? Kid, believe it or not, we're not here to talk.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:42.960
Hey, wait!

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.300
You know him?

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.330
Shut up!

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.330
Oh...

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:48.530
Hey! We need to talk.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.160
Sorry, but...

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.760
Hey! What's the big idea, Odelo?!

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:56.700
What's gotten into you?!

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:58.530
If you're looking for your dad,

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.130
do it where Suzy and Warren can't see!

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:05.300
And trying to brown-nose that Federation scum!

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.500
Don't you know how unsightly it is?!

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.330
I'm not brown-nosing them!

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.660
There's something I want to ask them!

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:14.300
You...

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:22.360
What, you can't fight when you're not in a mobile suit?!

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.030
What was that?!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:26.660
Why, you!

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.260
Something wrong with what I said?!

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.260
Yeah!

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.360
A fight?

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:39.230
According to Dupré company,

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:42.800
the League Militaire have strengthened their forces.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.500
They were moving south as they fought...

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.160
Moving south?

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.600
You can tell from how the blast craters overlap...

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.060
...and the direction of the beam scars.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:58.660
Contact Largaine. Also, are there any towns nearby?

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.400
Let's take a break.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:07.530
You don't care at all about Warren and Suzy's feelings?!

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.260
I do! I do!

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:11.730
You!

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.360
That dirty old man! It's disgusting!

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.660
Now you've done it!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:18.960
That's nothing!

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.260
You won't beat me!

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:21.930
You...

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.000
What's up? Oh, a fight?

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:27.460
Helen, which do you think will win?

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:29.760
Will you bet your earrings, Junko?

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:32.500
Okay, if you bet your new lipstick.

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.600
Okay, with a kiss, too.

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:37.900
You!

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:39.830
Stop it!

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:47.030
Why, you...

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.200
Screw this!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.260
Thanks.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.330
Why would you do something so violent?

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:05.600
Leave me alone.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:09.860
I get your earrings!

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.560
Junko loses.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.760
Wow, Odelo was great!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.000
Üso wasn't bad, either!

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.100
Well, that's how boys are.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:17.800
Yeah!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.630
Sorry to trouble you, Ensign.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:21.660
It's quite all right.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.500
To make your acquaintance, please have a drink.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:28.800
Thanks.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:33.260
Seen any trucks loaded with mobile suits around here lately?

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.800
I saw one headed south through the forest half a day ago.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:37.900
Stop that!

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:38.900
South...

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:43.460
There's a pre-UC airfield there, at old Bechyne!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.760
Call for reinforcements!

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:45.460
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:51.130
Sorry to disturb you.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:56.060
Oh, that's right.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:08.860
We never knew Hangerg had a son living in Kasarelia.

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:12.000
Your father was a careful man.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:16.800
So, my dad was involved in setting up the League Militaire, huh?

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:20.760
Yes, by appealing to his colleagues in the Federation Forces.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.960
Where is he?

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:24.130
We don't know if he's alive or dead.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:28.730
If he got careless, he'd be first in line for the guillotine.

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:31.660
Maybe that Jinn Jahannam guy would know.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:34.060
He wouldn't have any news of Hangerg.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:36.260
What about my mother, Myra Miggelle?

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.860
I don't know.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:39.530
I understand how you feel,

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:41.760
but rushing into things will just get you hurt.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.760
Roger. I'll move it into the hangar.

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:10.030
Your dad's with the transport corporation at Arti Gibraltar, right?

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.700
Maybe, but I'm not sure.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:16.930
The corporation there controls the Euro zone, right?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.860
It think it'd be worth checking out.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:21.560
Odelo!

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:35.360
The setters have all left! Until the transport takes off...

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.730
We'll defend it, no matter what!

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:39.200
That was our original mission, after all.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.700
Peggie, Kite, Cony, you got that?

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:42.430
Okay!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:43.400
Okay! Right!

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.160
Dammit, here they come!

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.700
Where's the Jamesgun team?! I'm taking off!

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:13.000
Can't we send out the mobile suits we've got in here?!

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:14.800
Not the ones that have been loaded!

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:18.430
You think we'll get out of here if we don't send them out?!

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:21.900
My duty is to transport those mobile suits!

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:24.400
I won't take orders to engage in combat!

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.060
The enemy isn't going to let you go, you know!

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:32.700
If you don't wanna get left behind, then do what I say!

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:36.000
If we casually stroll out of here, we'll be killed!

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:36.830
Miss Marbet!

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.630
Odelo, the plane's taking off!

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:40.200
We've got a few enemies out here!

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:42.030
If we don't fight back, we're finished!

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.730
Where are the Jamesguns?

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.400
They don't stand a chance!

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:49.830
Where's Shahkti? Flanders and Haro are missing, too!

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.400
Didn't she go with you?

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:52.830
They were just here.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:54.660
All they do is cause trouble!

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.260
Hey, what are you doing?!

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.260
Üso!

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:01.200
The battle has started!

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.330
No! You can't go out there!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:05.730
Üso!

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.260
He said Shahkti's missing!

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:09.860
Marbet!

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.200
Moving out.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:23.160
Use the radio and flares to alert Lupe Cineau's unit.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.530
Launching signal flares.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:28.330
But let's have our Gattarl Team settle this before they arrive.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:48.400
Our Gattarl Team reinforcements are already attacking?

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.900
I guess Duker Iq is the lucky one today.

00:12:59.930 --> 00:13:01.000
Over there, too!

00:13:03.030 --> 00:13:03.900
How could they!

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:05.960
It's like waiting to get killed!

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:08.260
It's a Shrike Team Gun EZ!

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:11.760
Junko and the others!

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.100
We'll look for Shahkti!

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:17.030
Üso, you get in your mobile suit and protect the transport!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:17.800
But...

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:21.760
If you don't, we'll never get to Arti Gibraltar!

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:25.000
Looks like the transport's leaving on runway 4!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.460
Gotcha. Odelo, I'm counting on you!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.460
Right!

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.360
Understood! I'll leave the payload hatch open!

00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:37.930
While I try to take off,

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:40.860
any mobile suits that can jump back on, I'll take!

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.160
Üso, take the one further in!

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:44.900
Right!

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.500
Be careful when you exit the hatch!

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:47.200
Right!

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:54.660
Odelo, please find Shahkti.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:09.000
This is no Jamesgun, pal!

00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:16.530
I'll handle the ones up here, Sis!

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:22.230
Üso, I'm sending you out! Okay?

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.200
It's moving!

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.060
Where are Marbet and Oliver?

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.000
There are even more enemies, now!

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.160
Miss Marbet! Mr. Oliver!

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.800
What's up with this bike unit?

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:45.500
Marbet, defend us on the ground!

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.230
Right!

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:51.430
Three Gundam replicas now? Interesting!

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:57.360
A transport's leaving on the runway on the other side?

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:07.030
PCST? A Public Corporation of Space Transport plane?

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:10.330
A non-political corporation shouldn't be involved.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.160
What's that thing doing here?!

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:24.600
Shahkti, this is no place to be planting flowers!

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:27.030
Shahkti! This is not a farm!

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.260
I hear Karl crying!

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:30.960
Shahkti!

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:36.500
What are you doing?! If you stay here, you'll be killed!

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.030
Odelo, hurry!

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:41.930
Right.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:44.460
Shahkti, get on!

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:45.460
They're here!

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.360
Shahkti!

00:15:58.700 --> 00:15:59.900
Shahkti!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.260
Shahkti! Shahkti!

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.700
Did they get the kid's suit?

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:28.600
Can the kid still move?

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:32.100
Odelo!

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:33.360
Shahkti!

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:34.900
Shahkti, stand up!

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.460
Karl's crying his eyes out!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.430
That's it, Shahkti! Go with the others!

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:43.600
Okay, here we go!

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:44.400
Okay!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.200
Odelo, take care of them!

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:51.960
A bit of panic with your girlfriend, huh?

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:52.660
Yes.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:56.300
Nice answer! Now defend the transport and let's get out of here!

00:16:57.460 --> 00:16:59.400
The transport's gonna be destroyed!

00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:00.760
No, it won't!

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:07.460
Romero, you find those kids yet?!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.060
Wait just a bit longer!

00:17:09.100 --> 00:17:10.930
Oh! That mobile suit!

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:14.530
Now I see.

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:20.560
It's a Federation transport plane camouflaged as one from the PCST!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:22.100
Here it comes! Take off!

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:30.300
Duker Iq, if you're down there, give me some support!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.730
The transport's taking off!

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:42.600
I'm not letting you do that!

00:17:47.430 --> 00:17:48.560
They got each other!

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.500
Oh, no!

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:01.360
She didn't stop the transport?!

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.930
Right! Kid, defend the transport!

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:09.160
The transport! Mr. Oliver! Miss Marbet!

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.830
They hit the engine!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:15.960
Can it fly?

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.960
Oliver and Marbet's units are acting as engines!

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:20.460
Hurry!

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.530
Get on! Escape!

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:30.030
Lt. Gomez, we've got them!

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:32.100
Even so, there are still enemies!

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.460
Come up to the upper cabin.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.530
Whew! Gimme a chance to breathe.

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:37.960
What about everyone else?

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:41.100
Doing extra work, thanks to us!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.460
You're more trouble than you're worth!

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:08.860
He used his docking function as a shield?!

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:13.860
Dammit!

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:38.600
We're short one machine, Peggie!

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:40.900
You can hear me through the skin touch circuit, right?

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.130
Who's missing?!

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:44.430
What's wrong, Peggie?!

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:47.730
Sis, Cony and Kite and I are here,

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:49.930
but Helen went off like a reckless idiot...

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:52.830
...and she let herself get too close to the enemy!

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:54.330
Helen?

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:57.160
The defining member of Shrike Team?

00:19:57.200 --> 00:20:00.530
Helen, the one who was most like an actual shrike?

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.430
You're telling me she was killed on the battlefield?!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.400
Lupe Cineau's team has withdrawn?

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:15.230
Yes.

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:18.400
Is that a Federation mobile suit with the Tomliat?

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:21.430
No, it's a modified League Militaire model.

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.300
Either way, they both had excellent pilots.

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:29.260
Yes. They killed each other without either of their main engines detonating.

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:32.660
One burned to death, and one crushed.

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:39.800
It means the League Militaire's firepower is intensifying and gathering.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.700
Commander Oliver!

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:52.330
Don't cry, Junko.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:54.900
We knew this day would come...

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:57.530
...from the moment we called Shrike Team together.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:20:59.660
So don't cry!

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.960
H-Hey, what did you say we're doing?

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:10.660
Fighting a state ruled by terror. That's all, Lt. Gomez.

00:21:10.760 --> 00:21:13.360
The Zanscare Empire's guillotines?

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:18.000
If we don't, that boy who pilots that machine like his life depends on it...

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:19.330
...won't be satisfied.

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.530
I'd just like to reiterate that I'd like your...

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:25.860
...League Militaire mobile suit team to protect our transport.

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:28.900
I'm glad to hear that from you.

00:21:29.730 --> 00:21:32.100
Does this course take us to Ireland?

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:34.060
What? No.

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:37.060
With those machines hanging on, we're headed southwest.

00:21:37.100 --> 00:21:38.260
Southwest...

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.000
We'll hit the Alps or the Pyrenees.

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:43.700
If we get past them, there's Gibraltar.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:45.330
Gibraltar...

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:46.600
Do you think...

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:48.430
Gibraltar?

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:53.330
In the letter Miss Katejina left for Üso,

00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:56.360
she wrote she was heading to Arti Gibraltar.

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:05.460
Father...

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:29.530
Piercing the sky, Blue lightning
sora wo tsukisasu aoi inazuma

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:35.320
Staining the earth, With the shadow of greed
daichi o someteku, yokubou no kage

00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:41.460
Once again, when the nightmare, Envelops the Earth
futatabi akumu ga, sekai wo tsutsumu toki

00:22:41.460 --> 00:22:46.790
You hear voices crying out "S.O.S."
"SOS" wo sakebu koe ga kikoeru...

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Let proud hope fill your heart
hokoritakaki kibou wo mune ni

00:22:54.720 --> 00:23:03.100
And stand up! Say a prayer for peace!!
tachiagare! heiwa no inori komete!

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:05.100
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:06.100 --> 00:23:08.980
In every age
itsuno jidai mo

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:14.570
...People take risks for freedom
hito wa jiyuu wo kakete

00:23:15.000 --> 00:23:17.000
WINNERS FOREVER!

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:21.240
The battle goes on
tatakai tsuzukeru

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:25.920
Fighting all alone in solitude
kodoku na made ni hitori...

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:35.500
The sight of a pretty lady makes Üso happy.

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:40.200
But then, suddenly, a guillotine is erected in front of a shop.

00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:45.730
BESPA intends to use it to suppress the people of this peaceful port.

00:23:46.830 --> 00:23:49.930
And that's when Üso fights once more!

00:23:50.430 --> 00:23:53.360
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.400 --> 00:23:54.030
Next Episode SMASH THE GUILLOTINE

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:56.430
"Smash The Guillotine"!

00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:56.460
Next Episode SMASH THE GUILLOTINE

00:23:56.460 --> 00:23:57.600
Please watch it!

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:59.360
Next Episode SMASH THE GUILLOTINE
